// Sources: studies/structure.typ (the preliminary structural study, every size assumed), data/open_items.csv, docs/OPEN_LIST.md (V11.0, 10–17 Nov 2026), docs/AIR_SYSTEM.md (the malqaf core).
#import "common.typ": *
#show: setup.with([Structural brief · what the engineer is asked to design and confirm], [An architectural coordination scheme, not a structural design: how the house is meant to be carried, as simply as possible, so the engineer starts from a coherent picture. Every size below is assumed. Drawings: `02_ground_floor_plan.pdf`, `03_first_floor_plan.pdf`, the DXFs; the full study `studies/structure.typ` → `output/structure.pdf` on the archive branch.], [structural engineer])
#set text(8.6pt)

#H[1 · The scheme]
- *A reinforced-concrete skeleton with block infill*, as Saudi contractors build every villa: columns hidden in the wall lines, beams at each slab, hollow-block or solid slabs. *Walls on walls, columns on footings:* every column runs from its own footing to the roof; nothing starts on a beam except the stair trimmers and two short first-floor walls over the men's majlis (§ 5).
- *Levels (to confirm):* GF ±0.00, FF +3.60, roof +7.20; the malqaf head to +13.20. Floor-to-floor 3.60 with a 0.20 slab and beams 0.40–0.55 total gives 3.05–3.20 m clear under the beams before finishes (X11).
- *Slabs:* solid 0.20 where the spans are small (the west band, the riwaq, the projection, the 4.7 m roofs); hollow-block ribbed 0.30 (25 + 5) for the 4.36–4.75 m bays of the east band and the men's majlis roof; the double-height living's roof a flat solid slab 0.22 spanning 4.7 m east–west, *no beam crosses the void*. The engineer may change the types (X14).
- *Stiffness, a proposal:* the west core (the lift shaft W1, the west shaft W2, the stair walls, RC 0.20) matched by an east box (the solid laundry wall on x 8.95 W3 and the step's two orthogonal walls as RC 0.20, in place of the cut wall W4) so the centre of stiffness stays near the centre of mass of the long pentagon (13.3 × 24 m). Not calculated: the engineer models the lateral system (frame + walls) for the wind and seismic cases of SBC 301 (X13).
- *Rule (owner, 11 Nov 2026):* every wall one straight continuous line; a jog only for a stated structural reason.

#H[2 · The grid and the columns]
Columns 0.25 × 0.50 in the inner wall lines, 0.25 × 0.60 in the 0.25 outer walls, the three colonnade columns round Ø0.30; 36 columns C1–C36, all to the roof. Coordinates in the plans' frame (x east, y south, metres).
